        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/2.0/sql/dialect/overview.md#L12-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8724de1a344cd0a0fc297a0115d31226e767cdaa83ddbd37c69350667e68ebc2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fab4a93f2d1040fea8de33ca1a1d9773",
      "statement": "As of DuckDB 2.0 identifiers can also be quoted with backticks, and duplicate column names are deduplicated as name_1, name_2.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/2.0/sql/dialect/keywords_and_identifiers.md#L15-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:075c6057391282e7bc9ca4b96b06e769af466ae4d42cdf75ae2d3b46393bd4cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d2f836cc9cfc41dd9af7fcb28c6ce518",
      "statement": "DuckDB identifiers, including quoted ones, are case-insensitive via ASCII comparison while preserving their original case; preserve_identifier_case became a VARCHAR option in 2.0.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/2.0/sql/dialect/keywords_and_identifiers.md#L86-L188",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0583e312f613f6c1d7705fc2225969f6cfa239696bcf79593332fdaffc23dcbd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1dd53bd57d4044e69aa36379422d861c",
      "statement": "Unlike PostgreSQL, DuckDB performs float division for integer / and follows IEEE 754 for division by zero, returning Infinity or NaN.",
